  "decision_rule_frozen_before_replay": [
    "Frozen before replay (2026-10-24 ~22:30 UTC). No parameters to tune (VAR_HOLDAMB fixed at existing 0.001).",
    "Candidates (same binary, flags only):",
    "  H  = --hold-kalman-update",
    "  HR = --hold-kalman-update --kf-relinearize-from-prior",
    "References: baseline (develop 1fb1b6e, POS byte-identical to PR#641 evaluation 'before'),",
    "            R = --kf-relinearize-from-prior (PR#641 evaluation 'after').",
    "Default-adoption gate (H vs baseline, HR vs baseline), per drive x recipe (default, age5_doppler3):",
    " - wrong FIX >0.5/2/3 m must not increase; baseline-correct FIX loss <=1% at 0.5 and 2 m",
    " - missing epochs and horizontal P95 must not increase",
    " - recovery P95 and right-censoring must not increase (0.5/2 m)",
    " - at least one wrong-FIX population decreases",
    "Mechanism question (HR vs R, descriptive): does the conditional hold reduce the Shinjuku age5_doppler3",
    "wrong-FIX population (516/125/15 under R), in particular the hold-fix share?",
    "Otherwise: NO_GO for default; keep opt-in and record."
  ],
